You are an expert in TypeScript, Node.js, Express, Vite, Vue.js, Vue Router and Pinia, with a deep understanding of best practices and performance optimization techniques in these technologies.

Project layout (ERP АММИР)
- `client/` — Vite + Vue 3 + TypeScript + Pinia + Vue Router SPA, Feature-Sliced Design: app, pages, widgets, features, entities, shared.
- `server/` — Express 5 API in TypeScript, modules under `server/src/modules/<module>/` (router + repository/service + seed). Data is in memory; no database yet.
- `shared/src/` — domain types and pure domain logic used by both client (`@shared/*`) and server (`server/src/shared.ts`). Put business rules here (permissions, validation, statuses), never duplicate them.
- `docs/` — living product context and agent handoff; update `docs/project-context.md` when module status changes.
- No Nuxt, no NestJS/Prisma, no second UI library.

Code Style and Structure
- Write concise, maintainable, and technically accurate TypeScript code.
- Prefer functional and declarative patterns.
- Favor iteration and modularization to adhere to DRY principles and avoid code duplication.
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError).
- Each file should contain only related content: exported components, subcomponents, helpers, static content, and types.
- FSD imports go downward only: pages → widgets → features → entities → shared.

Naming Conventions
- Use lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., components/auth-wizard).
- Favor named exports for functions.

TypeScript Usage
- Prefer interfaces over types for object shapes.
- Avoid enums; use const maps or unions of string literals.
- Client code must satisfy `erasableSyntaxOnly` (no parameter properties, no enums, no namespaces).
- Relative imports inside `shared/src` and `server/src` use `.js` extensions (NodeNext).

Syntax and Formatting
- Use the "function" keyword for pure functions.
- Always use the Vue Composition API script setup style for Vue components.

UI and Styling
- Style with scoped CSS and the CSS custom properties from `client/src/app/styles/index.css` (Montserrat, midnight/dodger palette, radius 2px, control height 44px). Do not invent new tokens.
- Используй только семантические токены из index.css; примитивы палитры в компонентах запрещены. No hex/rgb literals in `.vue` files.
- Цвета — только семантические токены; новые цвета добавляются парой для светлой и тёмной темы в `index.css`. No `[data-theme` selectors in components — add a semantic token instead.
- Reuse shared classes (`.ui-badge--*`, `.ui-table`, `.ui-segmented`, `.ui-sheet`, `.ui-form*`) and `shared/ui` components/icons (inline SVG, no icon packages).
- Hover styles only inside `@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)`; tap targets ≥ 44px.
- Do not introduce Tailwind, Element Plus, or other UI kits.
- UI copy is Russian only.
- Breakpoints: 560 (phone), 860 (main mobile breakpoint), 1280 (full sidebar); keep layouts usable on mobile.

API and data
- All client data goes through `client/src/shared/api/http.ts`; the current role is sent in the `x-erp-role` header.
- The server is the source of truth for permissions and PII filtering (СНИЛС и т.п. — только роль «Админ»).
- Bitrix (Disk, auth, write-back) stays mocked until real integration is agreed.

Don't:
- Don't add comments unless they explain a non-obvious constraint.
- Don't catch errors silently — surface them to the user or re-throw.
- Don't install new dependencies without explicit ask.
- Don't touch package.json unless the task requires it.

Tests:
- Node's built-in test runner via `tsx --test` (`npm test`); tests live next to code as `*.test.ts` in `shared/src` and `server/src`.
- New pure logic in `shared/src` — write the test with the code.
- Run `npm run check` (typecheck + tests) before finishing a task.
